      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. Let me write an improved, more understandable version of the test.Now I have everything I need. The test verifies that writing a single character (8192 = Unicode `\\u2000`) to an `XmlStreamWriter` with a null `OutputStream` doesn't throw — because the character is buffered in the prolog writer (prolog detection requires ≥5 chars), so the null stream is never touched. Default encoding stays \"UTF-8\".\n\nI'll improve understandability by: removing unused imports, renaming the auto-generated variable, and adding a brief comment explaining the intent.The improved test compiled successfully — `COMPILE_OK`."
